IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `wrca-dates`
IMPORT `wrca-core`

-- Workers Rehabilitation and Compensation Act 1988 (Tas) -- cases for the dates module and the seat-neutral core.
--
-- Every expected value is worked by hand from the deposited text, with the arithmetic in the comment above the
-- assertion. The basic salary is ILLUSTRATIVE: $1,200 a week (the gazetted figure is not deposited), so a unit is $1,200
-- and 415 units are $498,000. Regulative rules are asserted with EVALTRACE ... EQUALS FULFILLED where the trace ends
-- FULFILLED, and #TRACEd with an "-- expect:" line where it ends in a breach.
--
-- The facts follow Mia, a full-time storeperson at a Hobart warehouse (Monday to Friday), born 15 June 1990, employed
-- since 1 July 2020, who hurts her back at work on Monday 2 March 2026 and is totally incapacitated from that day. She
-- tells her supervisor that day and her claim, with its certificate, reaches the employer on Wednesday 11 March 2026.
-- Others vary one fact at a time.

`BS` MEANS 1200

§ `The dates module`

-- Monday 2 March 2026 and Monday 26 October 2026 (1 January 2026 is a Thursday).
#ASSERT `the weekday number of` (`the calendar date` 2 3 2026) EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `the weekday number of` (`the calendar date` 26 10 2026) EQUALS 1
-- 2 March 2026 plus 6 months is 2 September 2026; 31 August 2026 plus 6 months is 28 February 2027.
#ASSERT (`the calendar date` 2 3 2026) `plus months` 6 EQUALS `the calendar date` 2 9 2026
#ASSERT (`the calendar date` 31 8 2026) `plus months` 6 EQUALS `the calendar date` 28 2 2027
-- 2 March 2026 less 12 months is 2 March 2025, 365 days earlier.
#ASSERT `days from` ((`the calendar date` 2 3 2026) `plus months` (0 MINUS 12)) `to` (`the calendar date` 2 3 2026) EQUALS 365
-- Wednesday 11 March 2026: 3 working days (Monday to Friday) are Thu 12, Fri 13, Mon 16; 5 end on Wed 18.
#ASSERT `the last of` 3 `working days after` (`the calendar date` 11 3 2026) `in a` `Monday to Friday` `with closure days` 0 EQUALS `the calendar date` 16 3 2026
#ASSERT `the last of` 5 `working days after` (`the calendar date` 11 3 2026) `in a` `Monday to Friday` `with closure days` 0 EQUALS `the calendar date` 18 3 2026
-- One closure day in the period pushes the 3rd working day to Tue 17; a Monday-to-Saturday or seven-day place reaches Sat 14.
#ASSERT `the last of` 3 `working days after` (`the calendar date` 11 3 2026) `in a` `Monday to Friday` `with closure days` 1 EQUALS `the calendar date` 17 3 2026
#ASSERT `the last of` 3 `working days after` (`the calendar date` 11 3 2026) `in a` `Monday to Saturday` `with closure days` 0 EQUALS `the calendar date` 14 3 2026
#ASSERT `the last of` 3 `working days after` (`the calendar date` 11 3 2026) `in a` `every day of the week` `with closure days` 0 EQUALS `the calendar date` 14 3 2026
-- Born 15 June 1990, 67 on 15 June 2057; born 29 February 1960, 67 on 28 February 2027 (reading in wrca-dates.l4).
#ASSERT `the day a person born on` (`the calendar date` 15 6 1990) `attains the age of` 67 EQUALS `the calendar date` 15 6 2057
#ASSERT `the day a person born on` (`the calendar date` 29 2 1960) `attains the age of` 67 EQUALS `the calendar date` 28 2 2027

§ `ss 3, 65 -- units, child, age`

-- 415 units at $1,200 = $498,000.
#ASSERT `the dollars in` `the s 67 and s 71 maximum in units` `units at a basic salary of` `BS` EQUALS 498000
#ASSERT `the basic salary for 1991` EQUALS 311.30
-- s 65 child: 15 is; 17 and a full-time student is; 17 and not studying is not; 21 and studying is not.
#ASSERT `a person aged` 15 `is a child under s 65, being a full-time student or not` FALSE
#ASSERT `a person aged` 17 `is a child under s 65, being a full-time student or not` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`a person aged` 17 `is a child under s 65, being a full-time student or not` FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`a person aged` 21 `is a child under s 65, being a full-time student or not` TRUE)
-- Born 15 June 1990: 35 on 2 March 2026, 36 on 15 June 2026.
#ASSERT `the age in whole years of a person born on` (`the calendar date` 15 6 1990) `on` (`the calendar date` 2 3 2026) EQUALS 35
#ASSERT `the age in whole years of a person born on` (`the calendar date` 15 6 1990) `on` (`the calendar date` 15 6 2026) EQUALS 36

§ `s 25 -- liability`

GIVEN a1 IS A BOOLEAN, a2 IS A BOOLEAN, a3 IS A BOOLEAN, a4 IS A BOOLEAN, a5 IS A BOOLEAN, a6 IS A BOOLEAN, a7 IS A BOOLEAN, a8 IS A BOOLEAN, a9 IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Liability facts`
`liability` a1 a2 a3 a4 a5 a6 a7 a8 a9 MEANS
    `Liability facts` WITH
        `the person works for the employer under a contract of service or a training contract`                          IS a1
        `the injury is a disease`                                                                                      IS a2
        `the injury arose out of or in the course of the employment`                                                   IS a3
        `the injury occurred in circumstances that s 25(6) says do not arise from the employment`                     IS a4
        `the employment was the major or most significant factor contributing to the disease`                         IS a5
        `the disease is an illness or disorder of the mind arising substantially from reasonable management action`  IS a6
        `the injury is attributable to the worker's serious and wilful misconduct`                                    IS a7
        `the injury resulted in the death or serious and permanent incapacity of the worker`                          IS a8
        `the injury was intentionally self-inflicted`                                                                  IS a9

-- Mia: a worker, a back injury (not a disease) in the course of employment: liable.
#ASSERT `the employer's liability under s 25` (`liability` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `the employer is liable to pay compensation (s 25(1))`
#ASSERT `the employer is liable under s 25` (`liability` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- Not a worker (an independent contractor): not liable.
#ASSERT `the employer's liability under s 25` (`liability` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `not liable: the person is not the employer's worker (s 3(1))`
-- Hurt on the drive home, not at the employer's request: s 25(6)(a).
#ASSERT `the employer's liability under s 25` (`liability` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `not liable: the injury did not arise out of or in the course of the employment (s 25(1)(a), (6))`
-- A disease to which the employment was not the major or most significant factor.
#ASSERT `the employer's liability under s 25` (`liability` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `not liable: the employment was not the major or most significant factor in the disease (s 25(1)(b), s 3(2A))`
-- A disease to which it was: liable. A mental disease from reasonable management action: not.
#ASSERT `the employer's liability under s 25` (`liability` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `the employer is liable to pay compensation (s 25(1))`
#ASSERT `the employer's liability under s 25` (`liability` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `not liable: a mental disease arising substantially from reasonable management action (s 25(1A))`
-- Serious and wilful misconduct: not liable, unless the injury causes death or serious and permanent incapacity.
#ASSERT `the employer's liability under s 25` (`liability` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `not liable: the injury is attributable to the worker's serious and wilful misconduct (s 25(2)(a)(i))`
#ASSERT `the employer's liability under s 25` (`liability` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS `the employer is liable to pay compensation (s 25(1))`
#ASSERT `the employer's liability under s 25` (`liability` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE) EQUALS `not liable: an intentional self-inflicted injury (s 25(2)(a)(ii))`

§ `ss 32, 37, 38 -- notice and the time for a claim`

GIVEN injury IS A DATE, died IS A BOOLEAN, death IS A DATE, deaf IS A BOOLEAN, employed IS A BOOLEAN, ended IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Claim timing facts`
`timing` injury died death deaf employed ended MEANS
    `Claim timing facts` WITH
        `the day of the injury`                           IS injury
        `the injury resulted in the death of the worker`  IS died
        `the day of the death`                            IS death
        `the injury is industrial deafness`               IS deaf
        `the worker is still employed by the employer`    IS employed
        `the day the employment ended`                    IS ended

`Mia's timing` MEANS `timing` (`the calendar date` 2 3 2026) FALSE (`the calendar date` 2 3 2026) FALSE TRUE (`the calendar date` 2 3 2026)

-- Injured 2 March 2026: the claim must be made by 2 September 2026.
#ASSERT `the s 32 deadline for the claim` `Mia's timing` EQUALS `the claim must be made on or before` (`the calendar date` 2 9 2026)
-- Claim made 11 March 2026: in time. On 2 September: in time. On 3 September: out of time; saved if the lateness came
-- from the employer's failure to give the s 33A notice, or other reasonable cause (s 38).
#ASSERT `whether the claim is in time under s 32` `Mia's timing` (`the calendar date` 11 3 2026) FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the claim is in time (s 32)`
#ASSERT `whether the claim is in time under s 32` `Mia's timing` (`the calendar date` 2 9 2026) FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the claim is in time (s 32)`
#ASSERT `whether the claim is in time under s 32` `Mia's timing` (`the calendar date` 3 9 2026) FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the claim is out of time: no entitlement to compensation (s 32(1)(b))`
#ASSERT `whether the claim is in time under s 32` `Mia's timing` (`the calendar date` 3 9 2026) TRUE FALSE EQUALS `the claim is late but valid: the failure was occasioned by mistake, absence from the State or other reasonable cause (s 38)`
#ASSERT `whether the claim is in time under s 32` `Mia's timing` (`the calendar date` 3 9 2026) FALSE TRUE EQUALS `the claim is late but valid: the failure was occasioned by mistake, absence from the State or other reasonable cause (s 38)`
-- A death on 1 June 2026: the claim must be made by 1 December 2026.
#ASSERT `the s 32 deadline for the claim` (`timing` (`the calendar date` 2 3 2026) TRUE (`the calendar date` 1 6 2026) FALSE FALSE (`the calendar date` 1 6 2026)) EQUALS `the claim must be made on or before` (`the calendar date` 1 12 2026)
-- Industrial deafness, still employed: no deadline yet, and a claim now is in time.
#ASSERT `the s 32 deadline for the claim` (`timing` (`the calendar date` 2 3 2026) FALSE (`the calendar date` 2 3 2026) TRUE TRUE (`the calendar date` 2 3 2026)) EQUALS `no deadline yet: an industrial deafness claim may be made while the worker is still employed by the employer (s 32(2))`
#ASSERT `whether the claim is in time under s 32` (`timing` (`the calendar date` 2 3 2026) FALSE (`the calendar date` 2 3 2026) TRUE TRUE (`the calendar date` 2 3 2026)) (`the calendar date` 1 10 2026) FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the claim is in time (s 32)`
-- Industrial deafness, employment ended 31 August 2026: by 28 February 2027; a claim on 1 March 2027 is not maintainable.
#ASSERT `the s 32 deadline for the claim` (`timing` (`the calendar date` 2 3 2026) FALSE (`the calendar date` 2 3 2026) TRUE FALSE (`the calendar date` 31 8 2026)) EQUALS `the claim must be made on or before` (`the calendar date` 28 2 2027)
#ASSERT `whether the claim is in time under s 32` (`timing` (`the calendar date` 2 3 2026) FALSE (`the calendar date` 2 3 2026) TRUE FALSE (`the calendar date` 31 8 2026)) (`the calendar date` 1 3 2027) FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the claim is out of time: proceedings for industrial deafness are not maintainable (s 32(2))`
-- Notice (s 32(1)(a)): given as soon as practicable and before leaving: met. Not so, but excused (s 37): excused. Not
-- given, no excuse: no entitlement. Industrial deafness: the notice rule does not apply.
#ASSERT `whether notice of the injury was given under s 32(1)(a)` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `notice was given as s 32(1)(a) requires`
#ASSERT `whether notice of the injury was given under s 32(1)(a)` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `notice was late or missing, but s 37 excuses it`
#ASSERT `whether notice of the injury was given under s 32(1)(a)` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `notice was not given as s 32(1)(a) requires: no entitlement to compensation`
#ASSERT `whether notice of the injury was given under s 32(1)(a)` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the notice requirement does not apply to industrial deafness (s 32(2))`

§ `ss 69, 70 -- normal weekly earnings and the weekly payment`

`all four overtime conditions` MEANS `Overtime facts` WITH
    `the overtime or excess hours were a requirement of the contract of employment`       IS TRUE
    `they were worked in a regular and established pattern and in accordance with a roster` IS TRUE
    `the pattern was substantially uniform as to the number of hours`                     IS TRUE
    `the worker would have continued to work them in that pattern if not incapacitated`   IS TRUE

`overtime not rostered` MEANS `Overtime facts` WITH
    `the overtime or excess hours were a requirement of the contract of employment`       IS TRUE
    `they were worked in a regular and established pattern and in accordance with a roster` IS FALSE
    `the pattern was substantially uniform as to the number of hours`                     IS TRUE
    `the worker would have continued to work them in that pattern if not incapacitated`   IS TRUE

GIVEN start IS A DATE, o IS AN `Overtime facts`, two IS A BOOLEAN, others IS A NUMBER, ft IS A `Full-time contract`, comparable IS A BOOLEAN, cnwe IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `Earnings facts`
`earnings` start o two others ft comparable cnwe MEANS
    `Earnings facts` WITH
        `the day the incapacity began`                                                                      IS `the calendar date` 2 3 2026
        `the day continuous employment with the employer began`                                             IS start
        `everything the employer paid for work in the relevant period`                                      IS 80000
        `the part of it paid for overtime or excess hours`                                                  IS 4000
        `overtime`                                                                                          IS o
        `the part of it paid at the employer's discretion as a bonus, gratuity or similar payment`          IS 2000
        `the part of it paid for special expenses of the employment or as travel, meal or accommodation allowances` IS 5000
        `the worker had contracts of service with 2 or more employers when the incapacity began`            IS two
        `the average weekly earnings in the other employments, added together`                              IS others
        `which contract is full-time`                                                                       IS ft
        `there is another worker of the employer doing comparable work`                                     IS comparable
        `that worker's normal weekly earnings`                                                              IS cnwe
        `the hourly rate of pay, without overtime or shift or other allowances`                             IS 30
        `the hours a week the worker agreed or was rostered to work in the pay period of the incapacity`    IS 40

`Mia's earnings` MEANS `earnings` (`the calendar date` 1 7 2020) `all four overtime conditions` FALSE 0 `none of the contracts is full-time` FALSE 0

-- Relevant period: employed since 1 July 2020, so the 12 months before 2 March 2026: 365 days.
#ASSERT `the days in the relevant period under s 69(14)` `Mia's earnings` EQUALS 365
-- Counted: 80,000 - 4,000 overtime - 2,000 bonus - 5,000 allowances + 4,000 overtime (all four conditions) = 73,000.
#ASSERT `the earnings counted under s 70(2)` `Mia's earnings` EQUALS 73000
-- Normal weekly earnings: 73,000 / (365 / 7) = 1,400.
#ASSERT `the normal weekly earnings` `Mia's earnings` EQUALS 1400
-- Overtime not rostered: 69,000 counted, so 69,000 x 7 / 365 a week.
#ASSERT `the normal weekly earnings` (`earnings` (`the calendar date` 1 7 2020) `overtime not rostered` FALSE 0 `none of the contracts is full-time` FALSE 0) EQUALS 483000 DIVIDED BY 365
-- Employed only from 1 September 2025: 182 days to 2 March 2026; 73,000 x 7 / 182 = 2,807.69...
#ASSERT `the days in the relevant period under s 69(14)` (`earnings` (`the calendar date` 1 9 2025) `all four overtime conditions` FALSE 0 `none of the contracts is full-time` FALSE 0) EQUALS 182
#ASSERT `the normal weekly earnings` (`earnings` (`the calendar date` 1 9 2025) `all four overtime conditions` FALSE 0 `none of the contracts is full-time` FALSE 0) EQUALS 511000 DIVIDED BY 182
-- Two employers, neither contract full-time: 1,400 + 300 = 1,700. This contract full-time: 1,400. The other full-time,
-- at 1,500 a week: 1,500 only (s 70(2)(d)).
#ASSERT `the normal weekly earnings` (`earnings` (`the calendar date` 1 7 2020) `all four overtime conditions` TRUE 300 `none of the contracts is full-time` FALSE 0) EQUALS 1700
#ASSERT `the normal weekly earnings` (`earnings` (`the calendar date` 1 7 2020) `all four overtime conditions` TRUE 300 `the contract with this employer is full-time` FALSE 0) EQUALS 1400
#ASSERT `the normal weekly earnings` (`earnings` (`the calendar date` 1 7 2020) `all four overtime conditions` TRUE 300 (`a contract with another employer is full-time` 1500) FALSE 0) EQUALS 1500
-- Employed from 23 February 2026, 7 days: s 69(2). A comparable worker on 1,250: 1,250. None: 30 an hour x 40 = 1,200.
#ASSERT `the period of employment is 14 days or less` (`earnings` (`the calendar date` 23 2 2026) `all four overtime conditions` FALSE 0 `none of the contracts is full-time` TRUE 1250)
#ASSERT `the normal weekly earnings` (`earnings` (`the calendar date` 23 2 2026) `all four overtime conditions` FALSE 0 `none of the contracts is full-time` TRUE 1250) EQUALS 1250
#ASSERT `the normal weekly earnings` (`earnings` (`the calendar date` 23 2 2026) `all four overtime conditions` FALSE 0 `none of the contracts is full-time` FALSE 0) EQUALS 1200
-- Employed from 16 February 2026: exactly 14 days, still s 69(2). From 15 February: 15 days, not.
#ASSERT `the period of employment is 14 days or less` (`earnings` (`the calendar date` 16 2 2026) `all four overtime conditions` FALSE 0 `none of the contracts is full-time` FALSE 0)
#ASSERT NOT (`the period of employment is 14 days or less` (`earnings` (`the calendar date` 15 2 2026) `all four overtime conditions` FALSE 0 `none of the contracts is full-time` FALSE 0))

GIVEN cert IS A BOOLEAN, total IS A BOOLEAN, rate IS A NUMBER, change IS A NUMBER, couldearn IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `Incapacity facts`
`incapacity` cert total rate change couldearn MEANS
    `Incapacity facts` WITH
        `the incapacity is supported by a certificate in the approved form`                                   IS cert
        `the incapacity is total`                                                                             IS total
        `the ordinary hourly rate of pay immediately before the incapacity`                                   IS rate
        `the ordinary hours a week the worker was engaged for immediately before the incapacity`             IS 38
        `the change in the ordinary hourly rate under the contract or industrial instrument since then`       IS change
        `what the worker is earning or could earn a week in suitable employment or business`                  IS couldearn

-- Mia, total: the greater of 1,400 and 32 x 38 = 1,216: 1,400.
#ASSERT `the ordinary time rate of pay for a week` (`incapacity` TRUE TRUE 32 0 0) EQUALS 1216
#ASSERT `the weekly payment under s 69` `Mia's earnings` (`incapacity` TRUE TRUE 32 0 0) EQUALS `a weekly payment of` 1400
-- At an ordinary rate of 40 an hour: 40 x 38 = 1,520, greater than 1,400.
#ASSERT `the weekly payment under s 69` `Mia's earnings` (`incapacity` TRUE TRUE 40 0 0) EQUALS `a weekly payment of` 1520
-- s 69(3): the ordinary rate rises by 1 an hour: 1,400 + 1 x 38 = 1,438.
#ASSERT `the weekly payment under s 69` `Mia's earnings` (`incapacity` TRUE TRUE 32 1 0) EQUALS `a weekly payment of` 1438
-- Partial incapacity, able to earn 500 a week: 1,400 - 500 = 900. Able to earn 1,600: nothing (not below 0).
#ASSERT `the weekly payment under s 69` `Mia's earnings` (`incapacity` TRUE FALSE 32 0 500) EQUALS `a weekly payment of` 900
#ASSERT `the weekly payment under s 69` `Mia's earnings` (`incapacity` TRUE FALSE 32 0 1600) EQUALS `a weekly payment of` 0
-- No certificate: nothing.
#ASSERT `the weekly payment under s 69` `Mia's earnings` (`incapacity` FALSE TRUE 32 0 0) EQUALS `no weekly payment: the incapacity is not supported by a certificate in the form the Board approved (s 69(1))`

§ `s 87 and s 69B(2E) -- when the payments stop`

GIVEN dob IS A DATE, injury IS A DATE, assessed IS A BOOLEAN, wpi IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Cessation facts`
`cessation` dob injury assessed wpi MEANS
    `Cessation facts` WITH
        `the worker's date of birth`                         IS dob
        `the worker's pension age in years`                  IS 67
        `the day of the injury`                              IS injury
        `the day of the initial incapacity`                  IS injury
        `the permanent impairment has been assessed`         IS assessed
        `the whole person impairment, as a percentage`       IS wpi

-- Mia, pension age 67 on 15 June 2057; injured 2 March 2026, more than 2 years before it: s 87 day 15 June 2057.
#ASSERT `the s 87 cessation` (`cessation` (`the calendar date` 15 6 1990) (`the calendar date` 2 3 2026) FALSE 0) EQUALS `the entitlement to weekly payments ceases on` (`the calendar date` 15 6 2057) `the worker attains the pension age (s 87(1)(a))`
-- Impairment not assessed: 9 years after 2 March 2026, 2 March 2035, comes first.
#ASSERT `the day the entitlement to weekly payments ceases` (`cessation` (`the calendar date` 15 6 1990) (`the calendar date` 2 3 2026) FALSE 0) EQUALS `the entitlement to weekly payments ceases on` (`the calendar date` 2 3 2035) `9 years after the initial incapacity (s 69B(1)(c)(i), (2E)(a))`
-- Assessed at 10%: still the 9 years. At 16%: 12 years, 2 March 2038. At 25%: 20 years, 2 March 2046. At 30%: s 87.
#ASSERT `the day the entitlement to weekly payments ceases` (`cessation` (`the calendar date` 15 6 1990) (`the calendar date` 2 3 2026) TRUE 10) EQUALS `the entitlement to weekly payments ceases on` (`the calendar date` 2 3 2035) `9 years after the initial incapacity (s 69B(1)(c)(i), (2E)(a))`
#ASSERT `the day the entitlement to weekly payments ceases` (`cessation` (`the calendar date` 15 6 1990) (`the calendar date` 2 3 2026) TRUE 16) EQUALS `the entitlement to weekly payments ceases on` (`the calendar date` 2 3 2038) `12 years after the initial incapacity (s 69B(1)(c)(ii), (2E)(b))`
#ASSERT `the day the entitlement to weekly payments ceases` (`cessation` (`the calendar date` 15 6 1990) (`the calendar date` 2 3 2026) TRUE 25) EQUALS `the entitlement to weekly payments ceases on` (`the calendar date` 2 3 2046) `20 years after the initial incapacity (s 69B(1)(c)(iii), (2E)(c))`
#ASSERT `the day the entitlement to weekly payments ceases` (`cessation` (`the calendar date` 15 6 1990) (`the calendar date` 2 3 2026) TRUE 30) EQUALS `the entitlement to weekly payments ceases on` (`the calendar date` 15 6 2057) `the worker attains the pension age (s 87(1)(a))`
-- Born 1 January 1970: 67 on 1 January 2037. Not assessed: 2 March 2035 first. At 16%: 12 years is 2038, so 1 January 2037.
#ASSERT `the day the entitlement to weekly payments ceases` (`cessation` (`the calendar date` 1 1 1970) (`the calendar date` 2 3 2026) FALSE 0) EQUALS `the entitlement to weekly payments ceases on` (`the calendar date` 2 3 2035) `9 years after the initial incapacity (s 69B(1)(c)(i), (2E)(a))`
#ASSERT `the day the entitlement to weekly payments ceases` (`cessation` (`the calendar date` 1 1 1970) (`the calendar date` 2 3 2026) TRUE 16) EQUALS `the entitlement to weekly payments ceases on` (`the calendar date` 1 1 2037) `the worker attains the pension age (s 87(1)(a))`
-- Ray, born 10 August 1960: 67 on 10 August 2027, less than 2 years after the injury: 2 years after it, 2 March 2028.
#ASSERT `the day the entitlement to weekly payments ceases` (`cessation` (`the calendar date` 10 8 1960) (`the calendar date` 2 3 2026) FALSE 0) EQUALS `the entitlement to weekly payments ceases on` (`the calendar date` 2 3 2028) `2 years after the injury (s 87(1)(b))`
-- Born 10 August 1958, past pension age (10 August 2025) when injured: still 2 years after the injury.
#ASSERT `the day the entitlement to weekly payments ceases` (`cessation` (`the calendar date` 10 8 1958) (`the calendar date` 2 3 2026) TRUE 40) EQUALS `the entitlement to weekly payments ceases on` (`the calendar date` 2 3 2028) `2 years after the injury (s 87(1)(b))`
-- An injury on 15 February 2023, before the 2022 amendments commenced: not covered. On 1 March 2023: covered.
#ASSERT `the day the entitlement to weekly payments ceases` (`cessation` (`the calendar date` 15 6 1990) (`the calendar date` 15 2 2023) FALSE 0) EQUALS `the cessation date is not covered` `s 87 as in force before 1 March 2023 governs an injury before that day, and that version is not deposited`
#ASSERT `the day the entitlement to weekly payments ceases` (`cessation` (`the calendar date` 15 6 1990) (`the calendar date` 1 3 2023) FALSE 0) EQUALS `the entitlement to weekly payments ceases on` (`the calendar date` 1 3 2032) `9 years after the initial incapacity (s 69B(1)(c)(i), (2E)(a))`
-- The bands.
#ASSERT `the s 69B(1)(c) band` FALSE 50 EQUALS `less than 15%, or not assessed`
#ASSERT `the s 69B(1)(c) band` TRUE 14 EQUALS `less than 15%, or not assessed`
#ASSERT `the s 69B(1)(c) band` TRUE 15 EQUALS `15% or more but less than 20%`
#ASSERT `the s 69B(1)(c) band` TRUE 20 EQUALS `20% or more but less than 30%`
#ASSERT `the s 69B(1)(c) band` TRUE 29 EQUALS `20% or more but less than 30%`
#ASSERT `the s 69B(1)(c) band` TRUE 30 EQUALS `30% or more`

§ `s 69B -- step-downs, (2A) and the floor`

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, first IS A DATE, unusual IS A BOOLEAN, suitable IS A BOOLEAN, notoffered IS A BOOLEAN, planhours IS A NUMBER, earned IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Week facts`
`week` n first unusual suitable notoffered planhours earned MEANS
    `Week facts` WITH
        `the week of the period of incapacity`                                                               IS n
        `the first day of the week`                                                                          IS first
        `there is medical evidence the worker cannot perform the usual duties with the employer`             IS unusual
        `there is medical evidence the worker can return to suitable alternative duties with the employer`   IS suitable
        `the employer does not enable the worker to undertake suitable alternative duties`                   IS notoffered
        `the hours worked in the week under an approved return-to-work or injury management plan`            IS planhours
        `the worker's earnings in the week`                                                                  IS earned

-- Mia's normal weekly hours: employed more than 14 days, 38 ordinary hours and 2 overtime hours on all four conditions: 40.
`Mia's hours` MEANS `Normal hours facts` WITH
    `the worker was employed by the employer for more than 14 days before the initial incapacity`        IS TRUE
    `the average ordinary hours a week the worker was employed for`                                      IS 38
    `the hours a week the worker agreed to work in the pay period of the incapacity`                     IS 0
    `the hours a week the worker was rostered to work in that pay period`                                IS 0
    `the average overtime or excess hours a week`                                                        IS 2
    `overtime`                                                                                           IS `all four overtime conditions`

-- Short employment: agreed 30, rostered 35, overtime 5 not rostered: the higher, 35.
`a new worker's hours` MEANS `Normal hours facts` WITH
    `the worker was employed by the employer for more than 14 days before the initial incapacity`        IS FALSE
    `the average ordinary hours a week the worker was employed for`                                      IS 0
    `the hours a week the worker agreed to work in the pay period of the incapacity`                     IS 30
    `the hours a week the worker was rostered to work in that pay period`                                IS 35
    `the average overtime or excess hours a week`                                                        IS 5
    `overtime`                                                                                           IS `overtime not rostered`

#ASSERT `the normal weekly hours under s 69B(2B) to (2D)` `Mia's hours` EQUALS 40
#ASSERT `the normal weekly hours under s 69B(2B) to (2D)` `a new worker's hours` EQUALS 35

GIVEN parttime IS A BOOLEAN, engaged IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Floor facts`
`floor` parttime engaged MEANS
    `Floor facts` WITH
        `the basic salary`                                                                                   IS `BS`
