§ `ss 67, 67A -- death`

GIVEN spouse IS A `Dependency`, wholly IS A NUMBER, partly IS A NUMBER, notspouse IS A NUMBER, others IS A NUMBER, home IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Death facts`
`death` spouse wholly partly notspouse others home MEANS
    `Death facts` WITH
        `the spouse or caring partner`                                                                       IS spouse
        `wholly dependent children`                                                                          IS wholly
        `partially dependent children`                                                                       IS partly
        `of those, the children who are not children of the spouse or caring partner`                        IS notspouse
        `other dependants`                                                                                   IS others
        `the worker was contributing to the maintenance of the home of members of the family`                IS home

-- A wholly dependent spouse and two children of the spouse: 415 units to the spouse, 498,000 (s 67(2)(a)).
#ASSERT `the s 67 lump sum` (`death` `wholly dependent` 2 0 0 0 TRUE) `BS` EQUALS `415 units, to the spouse or caring partner (s 67(2)(a))` 498000
-- A wholly dependent spouse and a child who is not the spouse's: proportionate shares, up to 498,000 (s 67(2)(ab)).
#ASSERT `the s 67 lump sum` (`death` `wholly dependent` 1 0 1 0 TRUE) `BS` EQUALS `for each dependant, an amount reasonable and proportionate to the degree of dependency, 415 units at most in all (s 67(2)(ab), (b), (ba), (d), (3))` 498000
-- A partially dependent spouse alone (s 67(2)(b)), or with children (ba): proportionate, up to 498,000.
#ASSERT `the s 67 lump sum` (`death` `partially dependent` 0 0 0 0 TRUE) `BS` EQUALS `for each dependant, an amount reasonable and proportionate to the degree of dependency, 415 units at most in all (s 67(2)(ab), (b), (ba), (d), (3))` 498000
-- No dependent spouse, two wholly dependent children: 498,000 divided equally, 249,000 each (s 67(2)(c)).
#ASSERT `the s 67 lump sum` (`death` `not dependent` 2 0 0 0 TRUE) `BS` EQUALS `415 units, divided equally between the wholly dependent children (s 67(2)(c))` 249000
-- One partially dependent child: proportionate (s 67(2)(d)). One wholly and one partially dependent child: not covered.
#ASSERT `the s 67 lump sum` (`death` `not dependent` 0 1 0 0 TRUE) `BS` EQUALS `for each dependant, an amount reasonable and proportionate to the degree of dependency, 415 units at most in all (s 67(2)(ab), (b), (ba), (d), (3))` 498000
#ASSERT `the s 67 lump sum` (`death` `not dependent` 1 1 0 0 TRUE) `BS` EQUALS `the death lump sum is not covered` `s 67(2) does not say how the lump sum is paid where some children are wholly and some partially dependent and there is no dependent spouse or caring partner`
-- Only a dependent mother: not covered.
#ASSERT `the s 67 lump sum` (`death` `not dependent` 0 0 0 1 TRUE) `BS` EQUALS `the death lump sum is not covered` `s 67(2) does not say how the lump sum is paid where the only dependants are not a spouse, caring partner or child`
-- No dependants, but maintaining the family home: s 67(4). Neither: nothing.
#ASSERT `the s 67 lump sum` (`death` `not dependent` 0 0 0 0 TRUE) `BS` EQUALS `for each member of the family, as partial dependants, an amount reasonable and proportionate to the degree of dependency (s 67(4), (3))` 498000
#ASSERT `the s 67 lump sum` (`death` `not dependent` 0 0 0 0 FALSE) `BS` EQUALS `no lump sum: the worker left no dependants and was not maintaining a family home (s 67)`

